{# IN·A4 — THE ONE NUMBER ON THIS PAGE THAT IS NOT ABOUT TODAY.

   It is here because an unpaid claim is what a community remembers. It carries
   no window at all: a claim approved in july is still unpaid in august, and
   scoping this card to a month would quietly forgive it on the first.

   THE TWO DIRECTIONS ARE NEVER ADDED TOGETHER — a fine is owed TO the authority
   and a claim is owed BY it. The design refuses to sum them and so does this:
   two plates, two figures, no total anywhere on the card.

   → UhifadhiLabs\Incident\Overview\IncidentOverviewContributor #}
{% set o = by.incidents.overview %}
{% set fines = o.finesDue %}
{% set claims = o.compensationUnpaid %}
{% set finesMonth = o.finesAssessedThisMonth %}
{% set claimsMonth = o.compensationApprovedThisMonth %}
{% set oldest = o.oldestUnpaid %}
<div class="c" data-w="in_money">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">IN·A4</span>Money outstanding<span class="src">· {{ o.currency }} · everything still owed</span></span>
    <span class="ao-by incidents"><i></i>incidents</span>
    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-bottom:6px;gap:14px">
        <div class="kpi">
            <b class="disp">{{ (fines / 1000000)|number_format(2) }}<em>M</em></b>
            <span class="sub">fines assessed and unpaid</span>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi hot">
            <b class="disp">{{ (claims / 1000000)|number_format(1) }}<em>M</em></b>
            <span class="sub">compensation approved, not paid</span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rln">
        <span class="fog">Assessed this month</span>
        <span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">{{ (finesMonth / 1000000)|number_format(2) }}M fines · {{ (claimsMonth / 1000000)|number_format(1) }}M compensation approved</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rln">
        <span class="fog">Oldest unpaid claim</span>
        {% if oldest is null %}
            {# AN EM DASH, NOT A ZERO. "0 d" would name a claim that does not
               exist; this area owes nobody anything today. #}
            <span class="mono d" style="font-size:11px">— · no compensation is outstanding</span>
        {% else %}
            <span class="mono w" style="font-size:11px">{{ o.ageLabel(oldest) }} · {{ oldest.reference }} · {{ oldest.zoneLabel }}</span>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="rln">
        <span class="fog">Claims waiting</span>
        {# THE DESIGN SAYS "HOUSEHOLDS" AND THE MODULE DOES NOT RECORD ONE. It
           records claims and the parties to them, and one household can be two
           parties, so counting households would be a guess dressed as a figure.
           The row counts what is actually written down and says which. #}
        <span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">{{ o.openClaims }} {{ o.openClaims == 1 ? 'claim' : 'claims' }} · {{ o.claimZones }} {{ o.claimZones == 1 ? 'zone' : 'zones' }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="use">The only number on this page that is not about today, and it is here because an unpaid claim is what a community remembers. It is <a href="{{ o.dashboardUrl }}">a link into the module&rsquo;s money board</a>, never edited here.</div>
</div>
